1
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:07,080
[Fragments of Truth]

2
00:01:07,080 --> 00:01:10,840
[Episode 7]

3
00:01:14,040 --> 00:01:14,310
Hello?

4
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:16,120
Any word on Da Fei?

5
00:01:17,710 --> 00:01:17,920
What?

6
00:01:19,920 --> 00:01:21,120
Then hurry and get me a boat.

7
00:01:21,120 --> 00:01:22,560
Let me get out of here.

8
00:01:23,640 --> 00:01:24,790
Don't worry.

9
00:01:24,790 --> 00:01:25,230
Once I get there,

10
00:01:25,230 --> 00:01:26,200
I'll pay you.

11
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:28,710
Okay.

12
00:01:38,070 --> 00:01:38,710
Where's the cash?

13
00:01:39,120 --> 00:01:40,040
Where did you hide it?

14
00:01:40,280 --> 00:01:40,710
The cash?

15
00:01:41,510 --> 00:01:42,560
Where is the cash?

16
00:01:42,710 --> 00:01:43,510
Where'd you hide it?

17
00:01:43,710 --> 00:01:44,150
Talk.

18
00:01:44,590 --> 00:01:45,560
Where's the cash?

19
00:01:46,310 --> 00:01:46,760
Talk.

20
00:01:50,040 --> 00:01:50,920
You filthy tramp.

21
00:03:15,800 --> 00:03:16,590
Ah!

22
00:04:32,680 --> 00:04:34,680
Good grief!

23
00:04:41,480 --> 00:04:43,310
The body doesn't lie.

24
00:04:43,870 --> 00:04:46,310
It is the most honest witness.

25
00:04:47,120 --> 00:04:50,680
Now I know who the killer is.

26
00:04:51,510 --> 00:04:51,830
You.

27
00:04:53,480 --> 00:04:54,720
If I had done it,

28
00:04:55,480 --> 00:04:56,870
I'd be the one who stole the evidence.

29
00:04:57,830 --> 00:04:59,720
But I never got near the body.

30
00:05:01,070 --> 00:05:03,630
Because you used everyone else

31
00:05:04,040 --> 00:05:05,510
as pieces in your plan.

32
00:05:06,270 --> 00:05:07,560
Without them even knowing,

33
00:05:07,870 --> 00:05:09,190
they unknowingly destroyed
evidence for you.

34
00:05:10,390 --> 00:05:11,190
No way.

35
00:05:11,360 --> 00:05:12,920
Someone used me as a pawn.

36
00:05:12,920 --> 00:05:13,950
Anyone can make a wild guess.

37
00:05:14,510 --> 00:05:15,270
Where's the proof?

38
00:05:15,720 --> 00:05:16,600
What's your reasoning?

39
00:05:17,630 --> 00:05:18,000
Hey.

40
00:05:19,800 --> 00:05:20,830
You could've used

41
00:05:21,040 --> 00:05:22,040
someone else to do the killing.

42
00:05:22,920 --> 00:05:25,480
But you were obsessed
with killing by hand.

43
00:05:25,920 --> 00:05:27,270
That's what exposed your mistake.

44
00:05:28,720 --> 00:05:30,240
This wasn't the primary crime scene.

45
00:05:30,800 --> 00:05:32,830
You exploited the villa's symmetry

46
00:05:33,120 --> 00:05:34,360
to move the body to the other room.

47
00:05:34,480 --> 00:05:36,310
That's why everyone's accounts had

48
00:05:36,680 --> 00:05:37,630
a six-minute discrepancy.

49
00:05:39,190 --> 00:05:41,800
Go to the matching room next door,

50
00:05:42,070 --> 00:05:43,750
the original crime scene.

51
00:05:44,510 --> 00:05:45,870
The evidence should be there.

52
00:05:46,920 --> 00:05:47,390
Exactly.

53
00:05:48,510 --> 00:05:49,510
Anything you do

54
00:05:49,720 --> 00:05:50,720
leaves traces.

55
00:05:51,430 --> 00:05:52,310
Anything that happens

56
00:05:52,630 --> 00:05:53,310
leaves ripples.

57
00:05:58,070 --> 00:05:58,920
I'm done pretending.

58
00:05:59,120 --> 00:05:59,830
Time to show my hand.

59
00:06:00,480 --> 00:06:01,190
I'm the killer.

60
00:06:06,870 --> 00:06:09,310
How can you join the deduction
when you're supposed to be dead?

61
00:06:09,800 --> 00:06:10,800
This is outrageous!

62
00:06:11,390 --> 00:06:11,830
Sorry about that.

63
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:12,480
I forgot.

64
00:06:13,430 --> 00:06:14,310
Teacher Ding.

65
00:06:14,560 --> 00:06:16,430
Did you two have some
kind of cheat code?

66
00:06:16,920 --> 00:06:18,240
The rooms were identical.

67
00:06:18,720 --> 00:06:20,360
Who could possibly notice that?

68
00:06:20,680 --> 00:06:22,040
I didn't cheat.

69
00:06:22,040 --> 00:06:22,630
Don't go making stuff up.

70
00:06:23,920 --> 00:06:25,040
We can't bring those two next time.

71
00:06:26,480 --> 00:06:28,120
I still had a ton of lines left!

72
00:06:28,310 --> 00:06:29,430
They ruined the whole game.

73
00:06:31,240 --> 00:06:31,800
My bad, my bad.

74
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:32,600
I'm not coming next time.

75
00:06:33,480 --> 00:06:34,480
There'll be a next time?

76
00:06:34,830 --> 00:06:35,430
For future meetups,

77
00:06:36,120 --> 00:06:37,430
let's just

78
00:06:37,750 --> 00:06:38,630
play cards.

79
00:06:42,400 --> 00:06:45,040
[Murder Mystery Game: Bond of Mirrors]
[Twin Mystery]

80
00:06:45,390 --> 00:06:46,120
Hey, handsome.

81
00:06:46,360 --> 00:06:47,070
Here's your drink.

82
00:06:52,190 --> 00:06:53,870
Looks like I chose the wrong place.

83
00:06:55,600 --> 00:06:56,680
As long as Teacher Ding likes it.

84
00:06:57,600 --> 00:06:58,510
Hey, listen.

85
00:06:58,680 --> 00:07:00,480
You never come to our meetups.

86
00:07:00,560 --> 00:07:01,680
Not even once.

87
00:07:01,950 --> 00:07:03,680
Getting to meet you isn't easy.

88
00:07:04,120 --> 00:07:06,560
So why invite me now?

89
00:07:07,870 --> 00:07:10,270
Do you have some ulterior motive?

90
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:12,070
What motive would I have?

91
00:07:13,040 --> 00:07:14,160
So you don't like me?

92
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:16,000
Am I really that bad?

93
00:07:16,720 --> 00:07:18,000
Come on, spare me.

94
00:07:18,480 --> 00:07:21,510
I keep bothering you
with psychology questions.

95
00:07:22,310 --> 00:07:23,390
How will you thank me?

96
00:07:24,750 --> 00:07:26,950
I passed a shop yesterday.

97
00:07:27,120 --> 00:07:28,360
I saw something

98
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:30,800
you'd probably love.

99
00:07:30,800 --> 00:07:31,560
So I bought it.

100
00:07:33,510 --> 00:07:34,070
It's for you.

101
00:07:39,310 --> 00:07:39,870
Wow.

102
00:07:40,190 --> 00:07:41,630
This mystery game is out of print.

103
00:07:41,720 --> 00:07:42,430
Where'd you get it?

104
00:07:44,390 --> 00:07:46,310
We met through a mystery game.

105
00:07:46,720 --> 00:07:48,070
I knew you'd love it.

106
00:07:48,680 --> 00:07:50,070
You got that right.

107
00:07:51,070 --> 00:07:53,040
If you ever need help, just ask.

108
00:07:53,630 --> 00:07:55,310
I'll be your personal consultant.

109
00:07:55,920 --> 00:07:56,240
Sure.

110
00:08:00,390 --> 00:08:02,040
[Donglin CID]
I'm not getting up.

111
00:08:02,040 --> 00:08:04,070
[Donglin CID]
You've watched us for days.

112
00:08:04,070 --> 00:08:05,680
Every last one of you.

113
00:08:05,680 --> 00:08:07,070
Did anyone go look for him?

114
00:08:13,270 --> 00:08:13,830
What's going on?

115
00:08:16,310 --> 00:08:17,630
She says her son is missing.

116
00:08:18,240 --> 00:08:18,800
She doesn't know where he is.

117
00:08:18,800 --> 00:08:20,800
She heard CID might help find him.

118
00:08:20,800 --> 00:08:21,630
Now she refuses to leave.

119
00:08:21,920 --> 00:08:24,720
She reported it to
Beiguan Station days ago.

120
00:08:24,830 --> 00:08:25,830
It's outside our jurisdiction.

121
00:08:27,600 --> 00:08:28,070
Let me try.

122
00:08:31,390 --> 00:08:31,680
Ma'am.

123
00:08:32,080 --> 00:08:33,510
The floor's cold. Please get up
and tell us what's wrong.

124
00:08:34,030 --> 00:08:35,390
I'm staying right here.

125
00:08:35,630 --> 00:08:36,600
So everyone knows

126
00:08:36,870 --> 00:08:38,600
the police don't help ordinary people.

127
00:08:40,080 --> 00:08:40,510
Uh-huh.

128
00:08:41,320 --> 00:08:41,670
Here's the deal.

129
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:44,270
I know people at Beiguan Police Station.

130
00:08:44,510 --> 00:08:45,150
I'll take you there to check.

131
00:08:45,320 --> 00:08:45,910
Get up and talk.

132
00:08:46,080 --> 00:08:46,440
Okay?

133
00:08:48,440 --> 00:08:48,910
All right.

134
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:49,240
Let's go.

135
00:08:49,630 --> 00:08:49,790
Come on.

136
00:08:50,320 --> 00:08:50,910
Easy now.

137
00:08:51,080 --> 00:08:51,320
Come on.

138
00:08:52,030 --> 00:08:52,360
Let's go.

139
00:08:56,120 --> 00:08:57,910
[Beiguan Police Station Notice Board]

140
00:08:57,910 --> 00:08:58,870
Officer.

141
00:08:59,510 --> 00:09:01,320
My pension comes on the sixth.

142
00:09:02,030 --> 00:09:03,670
Today is already the 10th.

143
00:09:05,320 --> 00:09:06,360
He hasn't asked me for it.

144
00:09:07,320 --> 00:09:08,240
Just for that alone,

145
00:09:08,510 --> 00:09:10,030
you can't declare him missing.

146
00:09:10,200 --> 00:09:10,670
Right?

147
00:09:11,240 --> 00:09:12,510
It's been four or five years.

148
00:09:13,120 --> 00:09:14,320
He never once missed

149
00:09:15,030 --> 00:09:17,080
taking my pension.

150
00:09:18,600 --> 00:09:19,670
Sorry about that.

151
00:09:19,670 --> 00:09:20,870
For making you come all this way.

152
00:09:22,320 --> 00:09:24,120
We can't do much with this old lady.

153
00:09:24,600 --> 00:09:25,670
As for Wu Jia,

154
00:09:26,360 --> 00:09:27,320
have you looked into him?

155
00:09:27,320 --> 00:09:28,440
No need to check.

156
00:09:28,670 --> 00:09:31,030
His nickname is Wogua. He's over forty.

157
00:09:31,480 --> 00:09:33,120
He's a notorious loafer around here.

158
00:09:33,480 --> 00:09:34,510
He'd been in before.

159
00:09:34,510 --> 00:09:35,790
After getting out, no better.

160
00:09:36,240 --> 00:09:37,840
Always causing trouble.

161
00:09:40,510 --> 00:09:41,790
His disappearance isn't enough
to open a case yet.

162
00:09:42,440 --> 00:09:43,080
What about this person?

163
00:09:43,080 --> 00:09:44,870
He has shady friends.

164
00:09:45,480 --> 00:09:47,440
Three to five days away is normal.

165
00:09:47,670 --> 00:09:49,270
First, there are no signs of harm.

166
00:09:49,440 --> 00:09:51,080
Second, no unusual financial activity.

167
00:09:52,120 --> 00:09:54,510
We can't file just on her word, right?

168
00:09:58,600 --> 00:09:59,030
True.

169
00:10:00,720 --> 00:10:02,270
It was a minor injury, Grade I.

170
00:10:02,630 --> 00:10:03,440
Yes.

171
00:10:03,870 --> 00:10:05,320
He did two years inside.

172
00:10:06,320 --> 00:10:09,240
He worked at a well-known club.

173
00:10:09,910 --> 00:10:10,870
Night Flight Club.

174
00:10:11,870 --> 00:10:13,080
I think that was it.

175
00:10:13,790 --> 00:10:14,720
You knew that?

176
00:10:18,030 --> 00:10:18,840
Oh, yeah.

177
00:10:19,120 --> 00:10:20,910
Anyone else besides his mom?

178
00:10:21,440 --> 00:10:22,510
Just his wife.

179
00:10:22,510 --> 00:10:24,120
She was said to be unstable.

180
00:10:24,320 --> 00:10:25,840
In and out of lucidity.

181
00:10:26,240 --> 00:10:27,600
She and her mother-in-law
don't get along.

182
00:10:27,720 --> 00:10:28,510
Now,

183
00:10:28,840 --> 00:10:31,080
the old lady rents a place alone.

184
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:32,630
And that crazy wife of his

185
00:10:32,630 --> 00:10:34,080
is obviously

186
00:10:34,440 --> 00:10:36,200
sleeping around.

187
00:10:36,440 --> 00:10:37,750
She must be keeping a boy toy.

188
00:10:38,080 --> 00:10:39,480
Before she married into the family,

189
00:10:39,720 --> 00:10:41,390
she sold meat.

190
00:10:41,600 --> 00:10:43,240
You'd better have proof
before saying that.

191
00:10:43,720 --> 00:10:44,870
She was just a young girl,

192
00:10:45,320 --> 00:10:47,320
at Xishan Farmers' Market,

193
00:10:47,720 --> 00:10:48,670
selling pork.

194
00:10:48,870 --> 00:10:51,200
Men swarmed around her

195
00:10:51,320 --> 00:10:51,550
every day

196
00:10:51,720 --> 00:10:52,870
while she sold pork.

197
00:10:53,240 --> 00:10:57,030
She and that boy toy
must've harmed my son!

198
00:10:58,510 --> 00:10:59,080
Ma'am,

199
00:10:59,240 --> 00:10:59,870
please calm down.

200
00:11:00,200 --> 00:11:00,960
Calm down.

201
00:11:02,480 --> 00:11:03,870
Can you go check their place?

202
00:11:04,510 --> 00:11:04,790
Sure.

203
00:11:05,510 --> 00:11:05,790
Let's go.

204
00:11:17,840 --> 00:11:18,440
Officer!

205
00:11:18,510 --> 00:11:19,080
Lao Li.

206
00:11:19,080 --> 00:11:19,390
Hey.

207
00:11:19,510 --> 00:11:21,550
This is Officer Han from CID.

208
00:11:21,870 --> 00:11:22,910
This is the community security guard,

209
00:11:23,080 --> 00:11:23,440
Lao Li.

210
00:11:24,200 --> 00:11:25,510
Hey there, Officer Han.

211
00:11:26,600 --> 00:11:28,550
You're here about the hauntings, right?

212
00:11:28,840 --> 00:11:29,360
Lao Li.

213
00:11:29,550 --> 00:11:30,510
Don't start talking nonsense.

214
00:11:31,030 --> 00:11:32,320
Mrs. Wu's son is missing.

215
00:11:32,320 --> 00:11:33,720
They're just here to get the facts.

216
00:11:33,720 --> 00:11:34,030
Oh.

217
00:11:34,790 --> 00:11:35,910
You mean Wogua?

218
00:11:36,270 --> 00:11:38,200
I haven't seen him in days.

219
00:11:38,670 --> 00:11:40,510
Want me to take you there?

220
00:11:40,910 --> 00:11:41,240
Let's go.

221
00:11:41,240 --> 00:11:41,630
Let's go, let's go.

222
00:11:41,630 --> 00:11:42,270
Let's walk and talk.

223
00:11:42,440 --> 00:11:42,720
Go.

224
00:11:43,390 --> 00:11:44,200
This way.

225
00:11:46,200 --> 00:11:46,480
Up ahead.

226
00:11:46,550 --> 00:11:46,960
Oh no.

227
00:11:49,080 --> 00:11:49,480
Lao Li.

228
00:11:49,480 --> 00:11:49,840
Yeah?

229
00:11:50,270 --> 00:11:51,910
Do you know what goes on in his family?

230
00:11:51,910 --> 00:11:53,270
Oh, yeah.

231
00:11:53,270 --> 00:11:54,790
Everyone here knows him.

232
00:11:55,240 --> 00:11:57,080
Ever since he got out of prison,

233
00:11:57,320 --> 00:11:58,750
he's done nothing but loaf around.

234
00:11:59,240 --> 00:12:00,150
Most days, he's drinking

235
00:12:00,510 --> 00:12:01,440
or hitting his wife.

236
00:12:02,030 --> 00:12:03,030
His wife was heavily pregnant.

237
00:12:03,870 --> 00:12:05,870
He beat her until she miscarried.

238
00:12:06,200 --> 00:12:06,670
See?

239
00:12:07,030 --> 00:12:07,360
Hey.

240
00:12:07,870 --> 00:12:09,240
Did no one intervene?

241
00:12:09,870 --> 00:12:10,870
Of course people intervened.

242
00:12:10,870 --> 00:12:12,480
Both police and neighborhood
officials came.

243
00:12:12,840 --> 00:12:14,200
But he'd just make a scene.

244
00:12:14,440 --> 00:12:15,510
At most, they'd detain
him for a few days.

245
00:12:16,320 --> 00:12:19,080
Chen Yun's family lives far away
in the countryside.

246
00:12:20,480 --> 00:12:22,390
She has no relatives or friends here,

247
00:12:22,870 --> 00:12:23,600
and she has mental health issues.

248
00:12:23,790 --> 00:12:26,120
If she left, she'd end
up on the streets.

249
00:12:26,870 --> 00:12:28,320
Ever since she lost the child,

250
00:12:28,320 --> 00:12:29,320
the whole complex has had no peace.

251
00:12:29,320 --> 00:12:30,000
Hey, hey, hey.

252
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:30,630
There's been constant trouble.

253
00:12:31,080 --> 00:12:31,720
Will this ever end?

254
00:12:31,790 --> 00:12:32,080
Hm.

255
00:12:32,240 --> 00:12:34,000
Just show them the
place, then come back.

256
00:12:34,600 --> 00:12:34,870
Right.

257
00:12:34,960 --> 00:12:35,670
Okay, sure.

258
00:12:35,670 --> 00:12:36,000
So...

259
00:12:36,240 --> 00:12:37,840
It's this entrance right here.

260
00:12:38,080 --> 00:12:38,390
Top floor.

261
00:12:38,960 --> 00:12:39,510
Go ahead.

262
00:12:40,120 --> 00:12:40,870
Sure, thanks.

263
00:12:47,320 --> 00:12:48,240
Oh no.

264
00:12:55,790 --> 00:12:56,150
Hey.

265
00:12:56,670 --> 00:12:58,790
What was that about a haunting?

266
00:12:59,270 --> 00:13:00,910
Old folks get superstitious.

267
00:13:01,240 --> 00:13:02,790
He came to report it before,

268
00:13:03,200 --> 00:13:04,550
saying he saw a ghost in the hallway.

269
00:13:09,240 --> 00:13:11,080
People still believe that stuff?

270
00:13:12,720 --> 00:13:14,030
Can't really blame Lao Li, though.

271
00:13:14,390 --> 00:13:16,720
Someone spread a rumor online

272
00:13:16,910 --> 00:13:18,670
that Chen Yun's
miscarried baby returned.

273
00:13:19,670 --> 00:13:22,390
It cried for its mother in the hallway
late at night.

274
00:13:23,320 --> 00:13:26,270
Young influencers came
to film paranormal videos.

275
00:13:26,720 --> 00:13:28,670
A developer once planned

276
00:13:29,270 --> 00:13:30,390
to redevelop this area.

277
00:13:30,840 --> 00:13:32,320
The rumors killed the project.

278
00:13:34,240 --> 00:13:35,390
See there?

279
00:13:36,030 --> 00:13:39,000
That's where Lao Li claims
he saw the ghost.

280
00:13:45,240 --> 00:13:47,080
The bloodstain was tested long ago.

281
00:13:47,870 --> 00:13:48,200
Dog blood.

282
00:13:50,720 --> 00:13:51,960
The old man's fooling himself.

283
00:13:55,600 --> 00:13:56,390
Ah!

284
00:13:56,840 --> 00:13:57,600
Their place is upstairs.

285
00:13:57,870 --> 00:13:58,510
Let's head up.

286
00:14:56,280 --> 00:14:58,340
♪I stand in a fire-tempered jungle♪

287
00:14:58,340 --> 00:15:00,280
♪Withered leaves fall
as my strength runs dry♪

288
00:15:00,290 --> 00:15:02,190
♪Dust swirls as I clench my fists♪

289
00:15:02,200 --> 00:15:04,000
♪I strategize, my faith my armor♪

290
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:06,340
♪My defiance spills onto concrete♪

291
00:15:06,340 --> 00:15:08,760
♪Even thick fog can't hide
my clear gaze♪

292
00:15:11,910 --> 00:15:13,810
♪Let neon turn to thorns♪

293
00:15:13,820 --> 00:15:15,710
♪Flying low as the stars shift and turn♪

294
00:15:15,710 --> 00:15:17,660
♪Escape the maze,
transcend the challenge♪

295
00:15:17,660 --> 00:15:19,780
♪The meter starts, breaking the silence♪

296
00:15:19,820 --> 00:15:21,790
♪A beam cuts through
a crack in the wall♪

297
00:15:21,790 --> 00:15:23,950
♪This rhythm and noise
echo through the streets♪

298
00:15:27,550 --> 00:15:31,030
♪Don't be afraid. No one will answer♪

299
00:15:31,030 --> 00:15:34,400
♪Why is that child crying?♪

300
00:15:34,630 --> 00:15:37,100
♪The shrinking scar on my arm♪

301
00:15:37,100 --> 00:15:38,710
♪Means I've grown up♪

302
00:15:38,720 --> 00:15:41,860
♪You can trust me when I say that♪

303
00:15:41,860 --> 00:15:45,350
♪The wound still aches♪

304
00:15:45,750 --> 00:15:50,110
♪Like a biting winter♪

305
00:15:50,110 --> 00:15:53,370
♪But a spark still glows♪

